I think it is making some assumptions about the reader's dialect of
English. In American pronunciation for instance, "joke" and "note" indeed
have a sound which could only be the "o" in Lojban. It is not necessarily
the preferred Lojban "o" sound, but it is too far from "a" and "au" for any
confusion. (This is one of the advantages of not having very many vowels!)

mi'e la latro'a mu'o

